1. Install Apache or Nginx on your Linux server and verify the installation by accessing the default web page via your browser.
=>Apache was already present from the previous steps. It was started with:
Bashservice apache2 start
Accessing http://localhost returns HTTP 200 and the standard “Apache2 Ubuntu Default Page: It works”.

2. Create a folder named myflipkart in your web server's root directory and place an index.html file inside it that displays 'Welcome to MyFlipkart Deals!'.
=>/var/www/myflipkart/index.html
  <!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>MyFlipkart Deals</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/myflipkart/favicon.ico" type="image/x-icon">
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to MyFlipkart Deals!</h1>
</body>
</html>

3. Update your web server configuration so that visiting http://localhost/myflipkart shows your custom index.html page instead of the default server page.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> For Apache, use the Alias directive; for Nginx, use a new location block.</em>
=># /etc/apache2/conf-available/myflipkart.conf
Alias /myflipkart /var/www/myflipkart

<Directory /var/www/myflipkart>
    Options Indexes FollowSymLinks
    AllowOverride None
    Require all granted
</Directory>
a2enconf myflipkart
service apache2 reload

4. Add a favicon to your static site by placing a favicon.ico file in the correct location and updating your HTML to reference it.<br><br><em><strong>Constraint:</strong> Use any small image and rename it to favicon.ico for this exercise.</em>
=>A small existing .ico file was copied and renamed:
Bashcp /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/pygame/pygame.ico /var/www/myflipkart/favicon.ico
The HTML already references it with:
HTML<link rel="icon" href="/myflipkart/favicon.ico" type="image/x-icon">
http://localhost/myflipkart/favicon.ico returns HTTP 200.
